        <p>He always titotight- of her as Helen or ttetitm-a4 ll;lired, for no one on board the " " iet detected tile friends' little coaasdy all oelieved impiicitly that the tall, skniler. girl with the grey-blue eycs.a.nd dark brown hair was the great heiress, and the pretty faiiy with the glint of gold in her tresies the humble oompaniim. But as no one knew the girls' Christian names ,it followed that they naturally assumed that those by which they heard thenx address each Other were correct, and, thus, though all would have declared with one voice that lichen's surname was Jasper, thevwould have been just as positive she was Ilefen too.</p>
        <p>"Oh ! heaven save us," prayed poor Stuart in his anguish. "Heaven, spare my darling 1" I And surely that prayer was heard, for at that moment a voice in some foreign tongue I hailed him across the water and Rouale Stewart knew that help was at hand.</p>
