      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-12_WidnesExaminer_art0035" n="art0035">
        <head>PAD GATE.</head>
        <p>PAD GATE.</p>
        <p>A SEWAGE SCHEME FOR THE DISTRICT.—The dis- tricts of Padgate and Pearnhead which are governed under one local authority have been seriously urged by the Local Government Board to sewer that district. The Parish Connell have several times considered the matter, but owing,to the large expense have postponed the matter sine die. The Local Govetnment Board however, will not allow the matter to remain in obey- once and threatened proceedings thererore, and the district will be compelled to take the matter more seriously than it hss done ,and make the sewer. The district is slowly but tirely increasing. new dwelling houses in varions parts being erected and this of course is making the question of sewering the district more essential. That tie district would become more popular as a residential one's obvious, for it has the reputation of being one of the healthiest—if not the healthiest— suburb of Warrington.</p>
      </div>
