      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-12_WidnesExaminer_art0041" n="art0041">
        <head>EP. WiillEMV Pillk Fed&amp;</head>
        <p>EP. WiillEMV Pillk Fed&amp;</p>
        <p>" The first warnings I had about my health were a bad taste in my mouth and a feeling that I was off colour,'" said Mr. G. Gabriel, a well-known outfitter and hosier, of BSA, :fosley-street, Nlanchester. For several years Mr. Gabriel has been seriously handi- capped by brokea health, and that he has now found new energy and strength is entirely due to Dr. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>" In my younger days," said Mr. Gabriel, " irregular and hasty meals led to violent and weakening attacks of stonvich disorders. I suffered for twelve years from Indigestion in a severe form. My tonemA was coated, especially in the- morning, and I felt heavy, and doll. I had no appetite; even a light meal left mel with a sense of having over-eaten.</p>
        <p>" As these symptoms developed I ate less and less., but still had acute</p>
        <p>pains in the chest. A wretched languor came over me which I could not throw oft ; I was always dead tired, with no strength, and had violent headaches.</p>
        <p>"Many doctors examined me, and they invariably said that I was the victim</p>
        <p>of chronic indigestion. I tried many remedies inVb the hope of finding relief from the pain and dis- Mr. G. Gabriel, of Manchester; comfort, but nothing Cured by benefited me. )r. Williams' Pink Pills.</p>
        <p>"When reading a newspaper one day I catue across details of °Aires by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, and decided to try them. [did, and soon felt great relief from the pains and distress after meals All languor and drowsiness quickly passed of, and I began to enjoy increased energy with renewed strength. The blood seemed to race through my veins, and I could tell that nay general health was rapidly improving. Before long I became a vigorous, active man, able to sleep well, in the best of health, and always fit for business. With Dr. Williams' Pink Pills I require no other medi- cine, for they keep me fit." It is to men who long for strength and activity that Mr. Gabriel's words are addressed. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills supply new rich blood, strengthen the nerves, and help the system to throw off disease. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills have cured Indigestion' Anasmia, Eczema and Skin Disorders, Rheumatism, Sciatica, St. Vitus' Dance, Paralysis, Locomotor Ataxy; also Ladies' Ail- merits. But only the genuine cure—those labelled Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People. Refuse the substitutes offered at some shops, and if in doubt send j 2s. 9d. for one box. or 13s. 9d. for six boxes, to Dr. j Williams' Medicine Co., Holborn-viaduct, London.</p>
        <p>Mr. F. S. Gilbert, the operatic tenor and proprietor of the Gilbert and Neilson English Opera Company, who is now in the Bankruptcy Court, stated duriag his public examination that he attributed his position to the fact that the public prefer cake walks and coon songs to Wagner and Verdi. " Accidental death "was the verdict returned on Mon- day at Poplar on a man who died from blood poisoning which followed a scratch on the neck from a cat.</p>
        <p>best thing about Fels-Naptha</p>
        <p>The best thing about Fels-Naptha is that it makes clothes whiter and cleaner and sweeter than do ordinary soaps. And, of course,</p>
        <p>that is</p>
        <p>the chief object of</p>
        <p>washing. And it does it with cold water, without boiling and with very little rubbing. Fels-Naptha does away with the slavery of tile boiler-Fire, the steam, the sweat, the smell, the worry, and most of the hard work of wash-day.</p>
        <p>We know it seems too good to be true, but you can easily prove it for yourself next wash-day and your grocer will give you back the 2. you paid for Fels-Naptha if you are not convinced..</p>
        <p>FELS-NAPTHA 39 Wilson Street London EC</p>
