        <p>COMMERCIAL FAILTYRES.—According to " Kemp's Mercantile Gazette," the total number of Commercial Failures recorded in England and Wales during the week ending Friday, April 6th, was 168, viz. :—New Bankruptcy Proceedings published in the London ,Gazette, 79; Deeds of Arrangement registered, 89. The respective numbers in the corresponding week of last year were : Bankruptcies, 118 ; Deeds of Arrangement, 95—total 213 ; being a decrease of 45. The total num- ber of Commercit.l Failures recorded during the 14 weeks of the present year is 2,407 ; the total number recorded in the corresponding 11 weeks of last year was 2,655, showing a decrease of 248. In view of the interest taken by the public in all th pertains to notable trials, the April issue of "The Windsor," containing no fewer than 30 cartoons of Bench and Bar celebrities (reproduced in colour from " Vanity Fair") is sure to be ia great demand.</p>
