        <p>A BAD BOY STORY. Of a bad Ilttle boy I have to relate, IVIto would, in suite 4.4 all Tie warning he got, swing on a gate, And had a very great fall.</p>
        <p>• He laughed—it was so silly he said, He knew that he Nyould not do it ; One fine day he tell Olt his head, Then he began th rue it.</p>
        <p>For many weeks he lay quite still In his own little room, la-pt dark ; He af;..rwaras heard he was N't'ry And lie rdways carried a mark.</p>
        <p>Be warned in time, little children dear, Before if is too late; Don't at the older, and wiser, jeer, And don't swing on a gate. ETHEL HOLT.</p>
