      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-12_WidnesExaminer_art0116" n="art0116">
        <p>England and</p>
        <p>Le Olympic Games.</p>
        <p>England will, after all, be well represented in the cyclirrz events at Athens next month. The contests will include two npaced sprint races, two unpaced tandem 'races, A 20-kilometres human- Paced race, and an unpaced road race from Athens to Marathon and back--distance, 52f miles. The National Cyclists' Union has selected A. E. Wills, W. J. Pett, J. Draper, and H. Crowther to ride for this country, with H. C. Bouffier as a reserve. A. Rushen and J. Matthews, a tandem pair, will also go independently. The entries are confined to amateurs, but the Greek Government will entertain the :visitors during their stay in Athens, and provide the greater part of the cost of travelling.</p>
