      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-12_WidnesExaminer_art0123" n="art0123">
        <head>Novelty in Pedals.</head>
        <p>A Novelty in Pedals.</p>
        <p>Users of rat-traps who dislike toe-clips will be glad to learn about a patent "Firm-grip Anti-toe- clip" pedal lately placed on the market. In lieu of the usual serrations on the front and back( plates of the pedal, there are three small steel spikes-- two in front end one behind--:which are designed to pre- vent any slipping of the foot either forwards or backwards, but at the same time do not hold the shoe in the event of a rapid dismount being necessary.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1906-04-12_WidnesExaminer_art0124" n="art0124">
        <head>Fashion in Handle-bars.</head>
        <p>Fashion in Handle-bars.</p>
        <p>Though for many years the 18-in, flat bar en- joyed general favour among speedy road-riders, there are now many users of bars 21 in. wide. For example, the popular North Road handle-bar, with its forward curve, drop, and return, has two advan- tages: it dispenses with the necessity for a forward lug, and provides an alternative position for the hands when the rider is not hurrying, thus afford* tn a comfortable compromise.</p>
        <p>HOY FOOTBALL.</p>
      </div>
